@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+---
+id: task-004-hourly-rentals
+type: task
+title: "Hourly rentals"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Request
+
+Customers can rent by the hour. `addEquipment` accepts an optional `hourlyPrice` (integer euro cents per hour).
+A rental shorter than a day that starts and ends on the hour is priced at the hourly price for each hour.
+An item without an hourly price cannot be rented by the hour.
+
+# Acceptance
+
+- `hourlyPrice`, when given, is a non-negative integer number of cents; otherwise `addEquipment` throws.
+- A period shorter than 24 hours, with both ends on the hour (UTC), costs hours x hourly price (no long-stay discount).
+- Such a period on an item without `hourlyPrice` is rejected by `quote` and `book`.
+- Periods of a day or more still need midnight ends; sub-hour ends are rejected.
+- Hourly bookings clash with overlapping bookings of the same item, like daily ones.
+- Tests under `node --test`.
